# Every change to this repository requires review from a maintainer.
#
# Merging is discretionary and stays with the maintainers — see
# CONTRIBUTING.md. Contributions are welcome; governance is not open.
#
# The owner is a team rather than a person so that reviewer load can be
# shared without editing this file for every change in personnel, and so
# the repository does not advertise a single point of failure to anyone
# deciding whether to depend on the specification. It may hold one person;
# the indirection is the point.

*                   @sigrix-io/postern-maintainers

# The normative surface. Anything here is a compatibility commitment the
# moment someone implements it, so it is called out separately from the
# repository default even though the owner is currently the same.
#
# examples/ belongs here for the reason CONTRIBUTING.md gives when it names
# examples/ and schemas/ in one breath as normative-adjacent: an example is
# what an implementer copies, so a wrong one ships wrong implementations
# rather than merely reading badly. Guarding one of that pair and not the
# other splits something the contribution guide treats as a single thing.

/SPEC.md            @sigrix-io/postern-maintainers
/VERSIONING.md      @sigrix-io/postern-maintainers
/schemas/           @sigrix-io/postern-maintainers
/examples/          @sigrix-io/postern-maintainers
